 "_provenance": {
  "FLZ": "Fateev-Lukyanov-Zamolodchikov arXiv:0905.2280 (J.Phys.A 42 304012). Convention: 2pi^2 lam phi = [a1/x + a2/(1-x)]phi - FP int phi/(y-x)^2, alpha_i = pi m_bare^2/g^2 - 1 = pi m_ren^2/g^2 (== this repo's alpha). Sum rules G^(s)+- = sum_n lambda_{even/odd n}^{-s} (s>=2); s=1 regularized G^(1)+- = sum [1/lambda - 1/(m+1)] (their Eq. 4.18). Table 3 digits are verbatim from the paper's text layer; closed forms (Eqs. 1.8, 4.19, 7.1-7.2) were re-evaluated and reproduce every Table 3 digit.",
  "LM": "Litvinov-Meshcheriakov arXiv:2409.11324 (Nucl.Phys.B 1010 (2025) 116766). Same alpha convention. Their Tables 1-2 list lambda_n (NOT 2*lambda_n) to 6 significant digits at alpha in {-0.5,-0.1,0.1,0.5}; converted here to 2*lambda = M^2/(pi g^2). Their exact alpha-dependent sum-rule formulas (Eq. 5.3-5.5 + Spectral-sums.nb) were parsed and evaluated to 20 digits; the printed Eq. (5.5) G3+ has a typo (5715 zeta(7) should be 381 zeta(7)) -- the notebook-consistent version reproduces their own Table 3 and is used here. Exact ratio d-/d+ = sqrt(2(1+alpha))/pi.",
  "retrieved": "2026-07-20, via arXiv full-text; every closed form cross-checked numerically against the source papers' own tables before inclusion."
 },
